FD_USER={0: 'Lives in calm, shallow pools and riffles. Eats fallen insects, small fish and snakes.', 1: 'Lives in streams under 15C, above masu trout. Eats insects, small fish and mice. Jumps well.', 2: 'Goes to sea and becomes a big masu salmon. Lives where pools and riffles alternate.', 3: 'Goes to sea and becomes a big redspot salmon. Lives below char, in faster water.', 4: 'Prey of masu trout and dace. Lives on gravel in calm riffles. Eats aquatic insects.', 5: "Often lives alongside char. Some enter lakes. Doesn't die after spawning like salmon.", 6: 'Goes to sea and becomes a sockeye. Lives in high lakes. The tastiest salmon, but spoils fast.', 7: 'Likes calm water. Young eat insects; big ones eat fish and mice. Feeds well at dusk.', 8: 'Eats almost anything that fits its mouth: insects, worms, shrimp, small fish, even mice.', 9: 'Lives in bays, lakes and lower rivers. Mainly eats plankton and algae.', 10: 'Likes still water, so lives in lakes. Hunts actively near weeds and obstacles by the shore.', 11: 'Lives in rivers and lakes. Chases small fish and eggs. An omnivore that gathers at carcasses.', 12: 'Likes deep still water. An omnivore eating bottom animals, shellfish, worms and weeds.', 13: 'Lives in pools of the mid river. Eats only live prey. Coos when spawning.', 14: 'Eggs are eaten by dark chub and others. Adults are eaten by eels, catfish, bass and birds.', 15: 'Small upturned mouth. Lives in lakes, ponds and lower rivers, mostly in muddy backwaters.', 16: 'Lives on sandy bottoms of lower rivers and canals. Always schools near the bottom.', 17: "Has no scales. Squeaks 'gi-gi' with its fin spines. Hides under stones by day, feeds at night.", 18: 'Sea-going masu trout. Runs upriver young and eats insects in deep pools until spawning.', 19: 'Lives in ponds and lower big rivers. Stays near the surface eating plankton.', 20: 'Lives in ponds and lower big rivers. Schools near the top and sometimes jumps. Eats plankton.', 21: 'Common in calm pools. Leans toward animal food: caddis and midge larvae.', 22: 'Pointed snout, upturned mouth. Schools below 5m deep. The tastiest of the carp family.', 23: 'Lives in clear shallows with gravel and big stones. Active at night. Eats crustaceans.', 24: 'Has 10 whiskers. Swims over mud or burrows in. Lives in paddies and wetlands. An omnivore.', 25: 'Lives in calm shores and weedy inner lakes, and in paddies. Leans toward animal food.', 26: 'Hides among rocks and under willows; fights over territory. Eats fallen insects.', 27: 'The most bottom-dwelling crucian. Lives on mud and sand. Likes bloodworms and algae.', 28: 'They say to fish crucian on the bottom. Eggs fertilized by dace or loach sperm still hatch.', 29: 'Its fin spines sting if grabbed. Lives under stones in clean riffles, slipping through gaps.', 30: 'Lives in calm ponds, lakes, paddies and canals. Schools, and hides when startled.', 31: 'Lives in weeds along calm shores. Likes plankton, insects and shrimp. Forms schools.', 32: 'Lives alone in calm weeds. A carnivore that swallows small aquatic insects whole.', 33: 'Lives in calm, clean, weedy water under 18C, mostly near springs. Builds a nest of weeds.', 34: 'A cold-water fish of calm streams and springs. Common in weeds. Builds nests of plant fibers.', 35: 'Likes muddy still ponds and thick weeds. Fierce - even bites people. Breathes air.', 36: 'Lives in lakes and ponds, schooling in mid-water. Strains tiny prey with its gill rakers.', 37: 'Lives on sandy-muddy bottoms of calm rivers. Greedy night feeder; bites small fish and frogs.', 38: 'Lives from brackish river mouths to lagoons, near seaweed reefs and breakwaters.', 39: 'Schools in big rivers and lakes. The only fish-eater of the carp family; leaps after fish.', 40: 'Lives in reedy bays and inner lakes. Mostly eats weeds. Bony and tastes grassy.', 41: 'Common on sand. Sucks in food with sand and expels it through its gills. Buries itself.', 42: 'Lives in lakes, ponds and nearly still canals on plains. Prefers muddier bottoms than pike gudgeon.', 43: 'Lives on sandy bottoms of mid-lower rivers and often burrows in sand. Tastes bad.', 44: 'Lives alone in calm weedy water. In summer it chases small fish and shrimp through weeds.', 45: 'Likes clean sandy bottoms of lakes and lower rivers; also in brackish water. Spawns in clams.', 46: 'Lives in deep parts of lower rivers and lakes. Eats shore plants like reeds and duckweed.', 47: 'Lives in deep parts of lower rivers and lakes. Mainly eats snails, shrimp and insects.', 48: 'Slender, fox-faced body. Lives in mid-lower rivers, lakes and brackish water, on sand.', 49: 'Lives on sandy-muddy bottoms near bay mouths. Sucks up small bottom animals.', 50: 'All go to sea. Young stay in brackish water; adults in bays. Swim low, eat shellfish.', 51: 'Lives in brackish rivers and bays on muddy sand, eating lugworms. Fattens in autumn.', 52: 'Schools in shallow coastal waters. Bites animal bait like lugworms. Quick, with sharp eyes.', 53: 'Named by size: Seigo, Fukko, Hane, then Seabass at 60cm+. Often swims up big rivers.', 54: 'Silver-gray with ruby eyes. Lives in brackish river mouths and bays. Bait: a 30cm carp.', 55: 'Settles on rock and gravel, eating algae off the stones as it rubs its mouth on them.', 56: 'Lives in calm mid-lower rivers, lakes, ponds and canals. Likes still water.', 57: 'Lives in mid-lower rivers, river mouths and lakes. Hides in mud by day, feeds at night.', 58: 'Digs holes in mid river and lake bottoms. Eats fish, shrimp and frogs. Lives above eels.', 59: 'Lives in upper to mid rivers. A greedy omnivore that may bite even a bare hook.', 60: 'Common on muddy bottoms under 50m. A greedy omnivore eating crustaceans and shells.', 61: 'Lives in shallow seas, mid rivers and lakes joined to the sea. Changes color to match the bottom.', 62: 'Lives on sandy-gravel bottoms and rocky shores. Puffs up with water or air. Eats any animal food.', 63: 'The male blows bubbles to make a surface nest. Guards eggs and fry, attacking other fish.', 64: 'Lives in lowland rivers and lakes near the sea. Likes warm muddy water and weedy edges.', 65: 'Redspot trout return in spring as redspot salmon, when azaleas bloom. Spawns in late October.'}
